$ SOFiSTiK MCP self-test 2: two HEA 200 cantilevers, 6 m, built from structural lines (SOFiMSHC):
$ SLN 7 in group 3 at y = 0 with 1 kN/m, and the parallel SLN 8 in group 4 at y = 2 m with 2 kN/m,
$ each fixed at x = 0 and divided into 6 elements.
$ Hand calculation: reactions = (1 + 2) kN/m x 6 m = 18 kN, fixed-end moment = w L^2 / 2 = 18 kNm
$ (group 3) and 36 kNm (group 4), largest tip deflection = w L^4 / (8 E Iy) (+ shear part) with w = 2.
$ Checks that the server finds exactly the beams of each line by SLN number and by group.

+PROG AQUA urs:1
HEAD MCP self-test structural line
NORM DC "DIN" NDC "EN199X-200X" COUN 49
STEE 1 S 355
SECT 1 ; PROF TYPE HEA 200
END

+PROG SOFIMSHC urs:2
HEAD MCP self-test structural line
$ GDIV 1000: group = element number // 1000 (sofimshc_1.pdf p. 3-13, "GDIV> 0")
SYST SPAC GDIV 1000 POSZ
CTRL MESH 1 ; CTRL HMIN 1.0
$ SPT NO X Y Z ... FIX: sofimshc_1.pdf p. 5-3 "SPT - Structural point"
SPT 1 X 0 0 0 FIX F
SPT 2 X 6 0 0
SPT 3 X 0 2 0 FIX F
SPT 4 X 6 2 0
$ SLN NO NPA NPE ... SDIV (<0: number of elements) GRP STYP SNO: sofimshc_1.pdf p. 5-14 "SLN - Structural line"
SLN 7 NPA 1 NPE 2 SNO 1 GRP 3 STYP B SDIV -6
SLN 8 NPA 3 NPE 4 SNO 1 GRP 4 STYP B SDIV -6
END

+PROG SOFILOAD urs:3
HEAD MCP self-test load
$ BEAM GRP <group> TYPE PZZ PA PE: sofiload_1.pdf p. 3-26 "BEAM - Distributed Beam Loading"
$ ("Instead of a number FROM you may enter the literal GRP and the group number at TO")
LC 1 TYPE 'NONE' TITL 'self-test 1 and 2 kN/m'
  BEAM GRP 3 TYPE PZZ PA 1.0 PE 1.0
  BEAM GRP 4 TYPE PZZ PA 2.0 PE 2.0
END

+PROG ASE urs:4
HEAD MCP self-test linear analysis
LC 1
END
